# ── Renamed articles: the old URL keeps its rankings ─────────────────────
#
# These live OUTSIDE the generated block above on purpose. article_builder's
# sync_redirects() rebuilds that block from the files on disk, so a rule for a
# slug that no longer exists there would be wiped on the next --all run.
#
# tomato-guide-karnataka was published as "tomato-guide-up": a Kannada
# Karnataka tomato guide sitting at a UP slug, because it was copied from the
# UP article and only its body was translated. The old URL was earning (189
# impressions / 11 clicks at position 4.8 in the 8 Jul-4 Aug window), so it is
# 301'd rather than dropped. Both forms are covered — the extensionless URL is
# the one Google has, and without these it would fall through to the
# /articles/* proxy below and 404 on the backend.
/articles/tomato-guide-up        /articles/tomato-guide-karnataka   301!
/articles/tomato-guide-up.html   /articles/tomato-guide-karnataka   301!

# ── Articles published from the admin panel (no deploy) ──────────────────
#
# The 98 committed articles are real files on this disk, and a rule may not
# shadow an existing file unless it is forced — so every one of them keeps
# being served straight off Netlify's CDN and never touches Render. An article
# written in /admin has no file here (it lives in Postgres and is laid down on
# Render's disk at boot), so it falls through to this rule and the backend
# answers. That is the whole no-deploy mechanism: one rule, shipped once.
# The hub is FORCED first, because /articles/index.html does exist here and
# would otherwise win — and the hub is the page carrying the card for every new
# article. The backend serves that same file with the new cards inserted.
/articles/  https://krashi-mitra-v1-mrp4.onrender.com/articles/  200!
/articles/*  https://krashi-mitra-v1-mrp4.onrender.com/articles/:splat  200

# Hero photos for those articles, same story: committed images are served from
# here, a panel upload only exists on the backend. Worth a rule of its own
# because a missing image does not fail loudly — og:image and the hub card
# would simply come up blank and nobody would hear about it.
/images/articles/*  https://krashi-mitra-v1-mrp4.onrender.com/images/articles/:splat  200

